# Stray logs (e.g. STARSLING_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG session captures) and the uv
# lockfile — local artifacts a bulk `git add` must not sweep into the repo.
# CI installs deps with pip, so the skill doesn't ship a uv.lock.
*.log
uv.lock

# Claude Code project-local config (skills symlinks, settings.local.json,
# installed slash-command copies under .claude/commands/, etc.)
.claude/

# ci-speedup gap -> catalog loop (maintainers-only, local). Holds gap captures
# from real ci-speedup runs where the LLM fallback fired (SKILL.md phase 4a): the
# captured third-party job log + the LLM analysis + metadata. Job logs can carry
# repo internals / tokens, so NEVER commit this directory; only the human-reviewed
# detector + test PR the loop proposes reaches the repo.
# See maintainers/ci-speedup/MAINTAINERS.md.
.ci-speedup-gaps/

# ci-speedup transcript self-improvement loop (maintainers-only, local). Holds
# raw session transcripts AND generated summaries of real ci-speedup runs against
# third-party repos — job logs / report context may carry repo internals or tokens.
# NEVER commit this directory; only the human-reviewed SKILL.md / references / evals
# PR the loop proposes reaches the repo. See maintainers/ci-speedup/MAINTAINERS.md.
.ci-speedup-loop/

# ci-speedup dogfood loop (maintainers-only, local). Holds full clones of the
# third-party repos the dogfood workflow audits plus their run captures — large,
# and may carry repo internals or tokens. NEVER commit this directory; git cannot
# restore it if deleted. See maintainers/ci-speedup/MAINTAINERS.md.
.ci-speedup-dogfood/

# ci-secure test/eval fixtures are stored CLOAKED (as `dot-github/*.fixture`
# sources) and materialized into real `.github/` dirs at test time by the
# ci-secure conftest. The materialized copies are runtime output — never
# tracked, so registry/marketplace scanners never see workflow-shaped attack
# strings in the repo tree.
skills/ci-secure/tests/fixtures/.github/
skills/ci-secure/evals/files/*/.github/

# `claude plugin eval` writes its run artifacts (aggregate-result.json,
# report.html, kept sandboxes) to `<discovery root>/evals/results/` by default —
# which for ci-secure is INSIDE the installable skill. Gitignoring them keeps
# them out of history, but note that gitignore does NOT protect the install
# surface: the `skills` CLI copies `skills/<name>/` recursively and would ship
# whatever sits there. Always pass `--output-dir` somewhere outside the skill;
# `tests/test_ci_secure_install_surface.py` fails if results land here anyway.
skills/ci-secure/evals/results/

# The ci-secure eval harness writes a failing session's full stream-json plus
# the file corpus it collected to `./skill-eval-logs/` (relative to the working
# directory, so the repo root on a local run). Those hold the verbatim
# transcript of an agent session — prompts, tool output, the rendered report.
# Never tracked; see maintainers/ci-secure/scripts/run_skill_evals.py.
skill-eval-logs/
